  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support for UNODCs normative work on the implementation and interpretation of the UN Protocol to Prevent, Suppress, and Punish Trafficking in Persons</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed funding will serve to increase the capacity of the UNODC as the custodian of the Protocol to Prevent, Suppress and Punish Trafficking in Persons, Especially Women and Children, supplementing the United Nations Convention against Transnational Organized Crime (Palermo Protocol). Continued funding will be used to support efforts of a senior-level legal expert to ensure that UN-prepared or funded anti-trafficking materials and UNODC programs are consistent with the provisions of the Palermo Protocol.</narrative>
  </description>
